## Phase 2: Paired pointer ownership

Goal: replace grid-only virtualization with atomic paired state and cleanup.

### Tasks

✔ Extend the pointer adapter state with current paired position, original raw
  coordinate snapshot, both original accessors, both patched accessors, and one
  cleanup entry.
✔ Refactor `set()` to accept normalized paired state and claim ownership once.
✔ Write both raw coordinate pairs on every set.
✔ Patch both `getMousePos()` and `getMousePixels()`.
✔ Add `sync()` for reapplying the active paired state immediately before
  native dispatch.
✔ Refactor `position()` to return or copy the full paired state without
  exposing mutable internal tables.
✔ Remove `with_interface_mouse()`.
✔ Make `clear()` and cleanup restore raw coordinates, accessors, and adapter
  state.
✔ Make restoration best-effort across independent accessor conflicts.
✔ Preserve button-state behavior and cleanup ordering.
✔ Update the cleanup probe so pointer activity represents paired ownership.
✔ Add unit coverage for:
  - first claim and repeated moves;
  - one cleanup entry across repeated moves;
  - both raw coordinate pairs during ownership;
  - both Lua accessors during ownership;
  - defensive copies from `position()`;
  - explicit `sync()` after simulated external raw-field changes;
  - exact restoration of valid and invalid original values;
  - operation failure;
  - grid-accessor conflict;
  - pixel-accessor conflict;
  - simultaneous conflicts;
  - cleanup continuing after a conflict;
  - button down/up behavior under paired ownership.

### Phase 2 exit gate

✔ No adapter path can change only one coordinate pair.
✔ No native dispatch path has a private grid-only coordinate mutation.
✔ Cleanup restores every state item it can safely own even when another item
  has an ownership conflict.
✔ Focused and full unit suites pass.
✔ Lua syntax and formatting checks pass.

### Phase 2 implementation notes

- The pointer adapter now owns one defensive paired position, one exact raw
  snapshot, both Lua accessor identities, and one cleanup entry. Repeated sets
  update the paired position without replacing the snapshot or cleanup entry.
- `set()` and `sync()` use the same internal writer for `mouse_x`, `mouse_y`,
  `precise_mouse_x`, and `precise_mouse_y`. Both patched accessors read the
  logical paired position instead of volatile raw fields.
- `position()` returns a deep copy, and the adapter copies every input position
  before retaining it.
- Restoration attempts all four raw fields and both accessors independently.
  Accessors replaced by another owner are retained and named in the cleanup
  failure after all safely owned state and adapter internals are restored.
- The grid-only `with_interface_mouse()` owner was removed. Mouse clicks,
  wheel input, button transitions, and subject clicks now resynchronize through
  `sync()`; temporary focus/tracking flags remain independently scoped.
- The cleanup probe now asks the adapter whether paired ownership is active.

